{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he fled.</b> The term בריחה (flight) throughout Scripture denotes a person's departure from a place when there is no pursuer — and this stems from apprehension of future harm. But a person's departure from a place because of harm already present, or because of a pursuer, is called ניסה (flight)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:46.393823363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}